{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":422,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","line":978,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Myers diameter and compactness]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0267}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index, def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  Let $(M^n,g)$ be complete and connected, with $n\\ge2$. If\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k$ for some $k>0$, then $M$ is compact and\n  $\\operatorname{diam}(M,g)\\le\\pi/\\sqrt k$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  The estimate in \\cref{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index} excludes minimizing geodesics longer than \\(\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\); Hopf--Rinow yields the diameter bound and compactness.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Myers diameter and compactness] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6d796572732d72696363692d67656f6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0267</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-myers-index\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-myers-index</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound\">↗ def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M^n,g)$\">$(M^n,g)$</span> be complete and connected, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n\\ge 2$\">$n\\ge 2$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k$</span> for some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k&gt;0$\">$k&gt;0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is compact and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$\">$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch The estimate in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-myers-index\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368362d6d796572732d696e646578\">section 3</a> excludes minimizing geodesics longer than <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$\">$\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$</span>; Hopf–Rinow yields the diameter bound and compactness. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-explicit-cover","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","title":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","label":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","label":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","title":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric","label":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-geometric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-explicit-cover","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-explicit-cover","label":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-explicit-cover"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Myers diameter and compactness]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0267}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index, def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  Let $(M^n,g)$ be complete and connected, with $n\\ge2$. If\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k$ for some $k>0$, then $M$ is compact and\n  $\\operatorname{diam}(M,g)\\le\\pi/\\sqrt k$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  The estimate in \\cref{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index} excludes minimizing geodesics longer than \\(\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\); Hopf--Rinow yields the diameter bound and compactness.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","title":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}